# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: idefindboards
# board: discover
# The editor looks for boards itself, and offers what it found.
#
# Boards are looked for when somebody ASKS: opening every serial port on
# a machine writes to whatever is on it, and those ports belong to other
# things until a person says otherwise.  So the offer sits where boards
# are used -- beside Run -- rather than in the shell at large, and this
# desktop was never told to look.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 10
menu-pick Programming
wait 10
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 250
expect-title Project
note nothing to run on yet, and the way to change that is offered here
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Look for boards
menu-pick Look for boards
wait 400
note what answered is offered by name, beside Run; asking again does not
note mount the same board twice, since a port this shell holds is left be
click 71 8
wait 10
expect-menu Run on tiku|Run on tiku-2|
menu-pick Look for boards again
wait 400
click 71 8
wait 10
expect-menu Run on tiku|Run on tiku-2|Look for boards again|Save on tiku|
quit
